The attached image shows that Nano-11 facilitates antigen transport to draining lymph nodes. Panel A displays flow cytometry dot plots, demonstrating the detection and phenotyping of OVA-positive cells within myeloid (CD11c+) and MHCII+ populations in draining lymph nodes at Day 1 and Day 2 after injection with soluble OVA, OVA+aluminum hydroxide (AH), or OVA+Nano-11. Panel B indicates that Nano-11 significantly increases the mean fluorescence intensity (MFI) of OVA within OVA-containing cells, suggesting a greater antigen uptake per cell. Panel C shows that Nano-11 also increases the percentage of migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) among OVA-positive cells, highlighting its enhanced targeting of antigens to these immunopotentiating cells compared to OVA alone or with AH.